<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Västgötalagen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1220</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Västgöta Law</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Västgötalagen, or Västgöta Law, is the provincial law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vastergotland">Västergötland</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. Its older version, probably written down in the 1220s and surviving in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> of about 1280, is the oldest Swedish provincial law and the oldest substantial text written in Swedish in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> alphabet. It records the rights of the province's assembly and the customs of a society still largely independent of royal law.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vastgotalagen.jpg" alt="Västgötalagen" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: None · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:V%C3%A4stg%C3%B6talagen_blad_21.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
